# Files and directories that must NOT appear in the distributed plugin zip.
#
# Everything listed here lives in the repository but has no business on a
# user's server. The WP.org directory listing assets in assets/ are published
# from the repository's own assets/ folder, never from the plugin package.

# Every dotfile and dot-directory, at any depth.
#
# This single rule is what actually keeps .gitattributes, .gitignore,
# .distignore, .github, .vscode, .idea, .DS_Store, .editorconfig and anything
# else beginning with a dot out of the package. Plugin Check reports every one
# of them as hidden_files, so the rule is deliberately broad rather than a list
# that has to be remembered. The named entries below are documentation.
.*

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
/.github
.distignore

# WP.org directory listing assets — published separately, never shipped.
# The leading slash anchors this to the repository root. Without it the pattern
# matches any directory called "assets" at any depth, which would strip
# admin/assets/ and ship the plugin with no CSS or JavaScript.
/assets/

# Project documentation, not user documentation
CLAUDE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md

# Tests and local tooling
tests/
scratch/
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
.phpcs.xml.dist
composer.json
composer.lock
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/
vendor/

# The build tooling itself, which has no business on a user's server.
/bin/

# Build output and scratch
.dist/
dist/
build/
*.zip
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
